    <GaugingStation location="Bridport" name="Asker" number="44003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump weir closed in 1980 and replaced by 44011.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Bypassed at stages above 0.5m, bypass flow is included in the CEH rating. Two peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Crump weir on channel dug as part of flood prevention scheme. Flow measured at this location 1966 to 1980. In 1980-1996 station was moved to site at Jessops Avenue (head control weir with relief weir), but no data available for this station. Station replaced by East Bridge Bridport (44011) in 1996.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Peak flows presented for the earlier record (1966-1980) have greater uncertainty associated with them than new site (1996-date).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural runoff to within 10% at Q95. Several mills operate sluices and hatches upstream of weir and regulate the flow.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Rapidly responsive catchment due to steep slopes on Liassic Clay and marl. No major changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Ratings pre and post station move fit to corresponding gaugings well." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Confident in ultrasonic derived rating limb." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
